  "content": {
    "id": "p46-q14",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "Jasmine has $\\$10$ in 5-cent and 10-cent coins in her change jar and counts 157 coins in total.\n\nHow many 10-cent coins does she have?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "43 ten-cent coins.",
      "worked": "Let $f$ be the number of 5-cent coins and $t$ be the number of 10-cent coins.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\nf + t &= 157 &&\\text{(1)}\\\\\n0.05f + 0.1t &= 10 &&\\text{(2)}\n\\end{align*}$$\n\nMultiply (2) by 20.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\nf + 2t &= 200 &&\\text{(3)}\n\\end{align*}$$\n\nSubtract (1) from (3).\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\n(f + 2t) - (f + t) &= 200 - 157\\\\\nt &= 43\n\\end{align*}$$\n\nJasmine has 43 ten-cent coins.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 50
  },
